WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.102
-Our first guest tonight is
an Emmy Award-winning actor,

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.937
writer, and co-creator of
the hit series "Ted Lasso."

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:08.608
The season two finale premieres
Friday on Apple TV+.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.277
He'll also be making his return
to "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.578
this time as host,

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.247
with musical guest
Brandi Carlile on October 23rd.

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:16.583
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.917
our very good friend
Jason Sudeikis.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.418
How are you, buddy?

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.086
-Hi, Seth.

00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:22.621
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:23.957
-Nice to see you, too.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.292
This doesn't -- it feels like...

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.793
I can't believe
this is on television.

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.229
-Yeah, right?

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:32.565
It seems, like, very shaggy
for a network television show.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.233
-Hey.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:38.071
-The standards are just dropping
by the day, my friend.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.405
-It's fantastic. It's great.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:40.973
And then it'll all
come back around.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.409
It's fine.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:45.411
-Now, I will say one of the nice
things about this year's Emmy,

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:48.748
not just the fact that you guys
won so many deserved awards,

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.116
but it did kind of feel
like a party again

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:56.122
after a year where it sort of
had a more maybe funereal vibe.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.091
And you looked like
a million bucks, my friend.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.592
I mean, I was happy
to see you win,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.594
but I was even happier
to see you in this tuxedo.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.095
You got some real good feedback.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.330
-I mean, yeah.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.664
I mean, starting right there
with Kate Winslet.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:06.733
She walked by me at some point,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.268
and just, like,
rubbed my shoulder.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.902
And I didn't know
if it was 'cause of me

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:13.239
or you know, the couch I was
wearing or what it was.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.075
But whatever worked.
You know, it worked.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.077
-This photo --
this grabs a moment

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.080
where a woman is just turning
to go like, "Bugga-wha?!"

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.249
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.585
-I'll take your word for it.
Yeah, I hadn't seen that photo.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.852
I remember that moment happening

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.521
from the first-person
perspective,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.355
but that lets me know
that I was right.

00:01:30.355 --> 00:01:31.824
It really did happen.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:34.694
-We had your wonderful co-star
and fellow writer on the show,

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.028
Brett Goldstein here last night.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:37.363
He was talking about, you know,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.864
it was the first time
he had been at an Emmys.

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:42.368
And how much dread he had
when the music started

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.871
and there was an expectation
of dancing.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.372
You were a little bit
more familiar

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.374
with what a room like this
would be like.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.376
You're a man who's not
afraid to dance.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.678
But were you aware of how much
you'd be on camera

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:54.180
over the course of the evening?

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.582
-Absolutely not.
No, when we got there, like,

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.083
our table was
front and center --

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.586
or, it was in the round,
but we were right there.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.089
And then my seat was literally
right up in front,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.591
which has never been my move.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.093
I'm much more of a back of the
classroom, you know, whispering,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.995
passing notes, you know,
doing shenanigans.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:12.132
And to be -- it felt,
yeah, a little bit like

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:15.301
I was, you know, mayor
for a little bit.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.303
Or, you know, like some sort of
where they usually put royalty.

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:20.973
And, so, yeah -- I mean, even
the fact that I had to --

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.641
I mean, I joked around.

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:25.378
I was sitting at the table,
and the stage was behind me,

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.480
and I was like, "What if I just
sat like this the whole time

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.983
and just didn't even
turn around?"

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.351
Just ate my little box
of food and...

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:33.887
But, yeah, we had no idea.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.220
I mean, Brett's already reticent

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.523
because he's, you know, British
and a writer.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:40.860
But then to ask him to be at his
first fancy thing like that.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.262
'Cause all the other ones, we've
been doing in this setting.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.731
-Yeah.
-We open up laptops.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:49.802
And now here we are around
a bunch of fancy folks,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.638
and they want us to dance
right away.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.473
And Rita Wilson set the bar.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.974
You now, and too high,
in my opinion.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.509
-Too high.
It's going to be a very hard bar

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.678
for the rest of us to meet, not
just for next year's Emmys,

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:01.514
but I think for all
in the future.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.516
-Yeah, indeed. Yep.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.519
-I want to ask about what must
be very nice for you

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.121
is the feedback, not just
from fellow actors,

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.691
from fellow comedians, but
so many in the world of sports

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.359
are huge fans of "Ted Lasso."

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.861
Ted Heads, I believe,
is the terminology.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.198
What are the coaches that you've
been lucky enough to talk to

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:20.733
about your show?

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:25.237
-Well, I mean, early on,
you know, Jim Harbaugh.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.073
He was helpful.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.574
I mean, I actually
reached out to him,

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.209
'cause I met him years ago

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:33.012
when he helped us out
on "Detroiters,"

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.782
the show that Sam and Tim did
with Joe and Zach,

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:38.985
and we stayed in touch.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:41.688
And asking him, "Hey, what do
you wear on game days?"

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.990
Like, "Do you show up, do you
bring a little duffel bag?"

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.058
And he's like, "No, I just show
up in khakis and a sweatshirt."

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.161
I was like, "Okay, well, that's
what I'm going to do."

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.895
So, you know, I feel like
there's part of him

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:52.598
that feels ownership
over the character.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.334
But heard back from him.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.870
But then some, like, some
really fun ones, you know,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.306
being a basketball fan but
Steve Nash and Steve Kerr.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.141
Steve's son Matthew actually was

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.610
one of our writer's assistants
last year.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.914
And this season we name-checked
him in the same episode.

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:12.050
Our little homage to
that father and son duo.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.922
But yeah, we also heard
Juergen Klopp was a big fan.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.324
You know, the Liverpool coach.
-That's a fan.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:22.261
I mean, the coaches who have
engaged with it are exactly

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.129
the coaches you want to have
engaged with it.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:26.732
-100%.
-And that must be the best.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.600
-Oh, especially when you know,

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.669
Steve Nash is a huge fan
of soccer.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:31.904
Knows the game
really, really well.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.338
He really liked
the commercials too.

00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:34.806
So he's been a fan for a spell.

00:04:34.806 --> 00:04:37.810
But, like, when you have people
from the soccer/football

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.880
community embrace it, you know,
like Thierry Henry --

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.717
or, you know, who else?

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.552
Oh, I just met Abby Wambach.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.622
Her and her wife Glennon -- or
her girlfriend -- I don't know

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.358
their relationship status,
but they were holding hands.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.793
You know, scuttlebutt.
You heard it from me.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.860
[ Laughter ]
I don't care.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.829
I'll put anybody on blast.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.198
Together. Ladies too.
I mean, there you go.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.332
-You're in the public eye.

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:01.934
If people want to hold hands
around you,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.469
that just goes out
to the public.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.604
-[ Laughs ]
That's right.

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.372
-You have the eye of the public.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.341
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:11.043
-But the fact that,
like, Abby gave --

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:14.547
Glennon told me that she gave
a standing ovation when we won.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.782
I was like, "That's great."

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:19.151
So that's great when we're even

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.420
pulling the wool over
actual footballers' eyes.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.691
-You gave a nice shout-out to
our former boss --

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.759
I guess my current boss, who am
I kidding? Lorne Michaels.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.228
You got out. I'm still here.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:32.031
-Not in two weeks.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.065
He brought me right back in,
the son of gun.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.201
-He did. That's true.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.403
-Oh, boy.
-But have you heard from

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.672
Lorne since you -- I mean,
I guess you're talking about

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:40.739
the fact you're going
back to host.

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:42.175
You must have heard from him.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.309
-I saw him after that night.

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:46.345
But, yeah, man, I didn't know.
That was a fun thing.

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:50.016
Bill Lawrence, you know, who
does the show with us was like,

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:51.684
"When you looked over there
and gestured to him,

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.319
did you know he wasn't there?"
I go, "No, no.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.820
That was real time."

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.290
Like, I brain-farted a few
people that I wanted thank

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.959
because I riffed on him
not being there.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:03.762
I was like, "Well, you know,
we'll make some toilet humor.

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:07.433
Make my folks proud
and move on."

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.803
After that he, you know, he gave
some pearls of wisdom

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.305
and was just excited about --

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:15.408
We hadn't announced
who the hosts were coming up,

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:18.177
so he was playing it cool there.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:21.614
-Was one of his pearls of wisdom
don't go to the bathroom when

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:24.683
one of your former castmates
is likely to win an Emmy?

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:28.187
-I mean, yeah, you know,
2021 hindsight we call it now.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.589
-Exactly.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:33.092
-No, he's always learning.
He's constantly learning.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:34.726
He's a work in progress.

00:06:34.726 --> 00:06:36.362
He'll tell you that
first and foremost.

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.464
[ Laughter ]
-That is Lorne.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:43.436
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.571
He's always like,
"I'm not there, Jason."

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.306
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.774
-"I got so much to learn."

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.577
-He always -- Yeah, he goes,
"I don't come into work

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:52.745
because I know who I am.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.347
I come into work
because it's 11:30."

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:58.117
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.919
Hey, I've seen the trailer.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:04.456
I'm very excited about this film
that I believe is out on Friday.

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:06.224
"South of Heaven."
-Yeah.

00:07:06.224 --> 00:07:08.828
-Very not "Ted Lasso."

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:12.798
It must be fun to sort of do
something noir-ish,

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.734
because I feel like I haven't
seen you do that before.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:18.937
-I know. No, it's not really
a spoiler just 'cause I won't

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:22.475
tell you when I do it
or who I do it towards,

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.010
but I shoot a shotgun
in this movie.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.211
-[ Laughs ] Right.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.479
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:31.150
But, no, it's great. Yeah.
It's me and Evangeline Lilly.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.517
A bunch of other folks.

00:07:32.517 --> 00:07:35.487
But, yeah, it's like in that
style, like, '70s noir.

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:38.090
You know, when Walter Matthau
would play like a badass

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.893
in the movies in the '70s.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:42.694
I'm looking forward for folks
to see it.

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:45.231
It is very different than
"Ted Lasso."

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:47.333
Even though I have
a Southern accent in it,

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.267
but, yeah, there's no soccer

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:52.872
and, you know, not as much
hugging and forgiveness.

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.240
-Yeah, less rewarding arcs.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.908
I'm guessing the arcs
are less rewarding.

